Instructions

Karo GitHub Doc Formatter

Format event plans, sponsorship schedules, deliverables, or execution checklists into clean, ready-to-commit Markdown files for GitHub repositories.

When to Use

When the user asks to format event deliverables, timelines, or notes for a GitHub repository.
When creating or updating a README.md, SPONSORSHIP_PLAN.md, or operational checklists.
Instructions

Structure output cleanly using GitHub-flavored Markdown:
Use # for the main title, ## for core sections, and ### for sub-sections.
Use markdown tables for multi-variable data (e.g., deliverables, tiers, dates).
Use interactive checklist syntax (- [ ]) for action items.
Use blockquotes (>) for notes, rules, and non-negotiables.
Enforce repository standards:
Provide the suggested filename at the top (e.g., docs/sponsorship-plan.md).
Include a brief git command snippet to help the user commit and push the file easily.
Keep prose concise, operational, and directly copy-pasteable.
